{
  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "Evidence: The multimodal model (config_016: pca_n2000 + resnet50, concat) achieves 52.7% accuracy, while image-only resnet50 (config_010) achieves only 20.8%. This ~32-point gap tells us RNA contributes substantially, but we cannot yet decompose how much of the multimodal performance comes from RNA alone versus genuine cross-modal fusion. Uncertainty: We lack an RNA-only baseline with the same encoder (pca_n2000) and profile setting (singleprofile) used in config_016. Question tested: config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) provides a clean ablation that isolates RNA performance. Why best next: If RNA alone ≈ 50%, the image adds little and future effort should focus on RNA encoders/fusion; if RNA alone ≈ 30%, the multimodal gain is genuine and investing in better image encoders or fusion strategies (e.g., weighted fusion, ViT) becomes prioritized. This single experiment resolves the most critical design uncertainty and directly guides all subsequent allocation decisions under the limited budget."
}

